package agentsdoc

import "strings"

// writeV04bSection documents what 0.4b adds for an authoring agent: the
// composition of a document (include and fragment, template and use, with,
// scoped ids, the limits and the messages) and the tools that show an
// expansion. It names no path of the repository, since the project briefing
// (ProjectMarkdown) is this same text. The current language's defaults are in
// the section of their own that writeV04bDefaultsSection writes; its form
// controls and `{path}` in a `<button>` are in the Notes.
func writeV04bSection(b *strings.Builder) {
	b.WriteString("### v0.4b: composition\n\n")
	b.WriteString("- `<include src=\"FILE\"/>`, in a `<tui>` without `version`, places the elements of another file where it stands: directly under `<tui>`, in a `<screen>`, in a container, or in a `<keymap>`. `src` is relative to the file that writes the include (a fragment's, to the fragment). The file's root is `<fragment>`, which takes no attributes (`V002`) and is `V001` anywhere but the root of an included file; it may hold several elements and other includes. Ids, styles, and data are shared, and the document is checked as if the elements were written where the include stands; a diagnostic about an element an include placed ends with `, placed by <include> at FILE:LINE:COL`. A cycle, a file outside the file system a `LoadFS` host gave the document, or one that cannot be read is `V006` at the include; a stylesheet, or a file whose root is not `<fragment>`, is `V020`; an include that fails inserts nothing and the rest of the document is still checked. A fragment is not a document: `dump`, `play`, `preview`, `ir`, and `inspect` give it `V005` (\"check it through the document that includes it\") and exit 2, while `validate` and `fmt` accept it.\n")
	b.WriteString("- `<template id=\"T\">` holds a piece of markup that is never drawn by itself, and `<use template=\"T\" with=\"path as alias\"/>` is replaced, when the document is read, by a copy of it built where the use stands. A template is a direct child of `<tui>` or `<screen>`, in the document or in a fragment (elsewhere is `V001`), may come after its uses, and needs an `id` (`V012`; a second one with the same id is `V004`). Its body is one or more elements, never `tui`, `app`, `fragment`, `screen`, `style`, `keymap`, `bind`, or `template` (`V001`), and no loose text (`V013`). A `<use>` is not a node: it takes `template`, `id`, `with`, `if`, `hidden`, and a static `class` (any other attribute is `V002`, except a prop its template declares) and, as content, only the markup its template's `<slot/>` receives (`V013` when the template has none); one without `template`, naming no template, or closing a cycle of templates is `V019`.\n")
	b.WriteString("- Ids in a copy are scoped by its use: `<use id=\"billing\">` makes the `x` of the template `billing__x`, and a use inside a template scopes by both (`billing__street__input`). Outside the copy (`to=`, `when=`, `focus=`, `#id` selectors, `focus:` steps, an event's `source`) write the scoped id; inside the template a `#x` means the element of the same copy. A use without an `id` whose template holds an `id` at any depth is `V012`; a `to=`, `when=`, or `focus=` that names a use, or an id that only a template writes, is `B005` with the scoped id in the message; the id of a use is an id of the document (`V004` when repeated), and the copies of different uses never clash.\n")
	b.WriteString("- `with=\"path as alias\"` (several clauses separated by exactly `, `) makes the alias stand for the path inside the copy: `{f.label}` reads `form.email.label` and `bind=\"f.value\"` reads and writes `form.email.value`; nothing is copied, and an input in a copy creates a missing path when it writes. A copy also reads the aliases in scope where its use stands (a list row's `each` alias), and a `with` path may start with one; an inner `each` alias that repeats such an alias shadows it inside the copy, while one that repeats a `with` alias is `V011` at that element (the copy is still placed). A malformed `with`, an alias written twice, or one already in scope at the use is `V011` and the use inserts nothing.\n")
	b.WriteString("- `if` and `hidden` on a use are read where the use stands (its own `with` is not in scope) and decide whether its copy exists; in a list `<item>`, an `each` container, or a table they are decided per row, and a missing path is one `B002` at the use. A static `class` on a use is appended to every top-level element of the copy, after the classes the template wrote and before its `class:NAME` guards. A `<column>` cannot hold a `<use>` (`V016`): to reuse a column or the row `<item>`, make it the template and put the `<use>` directly in the `<table>`; its `if`/`hidden` stay per table, and a `with` path that starts with the row alias is read for every row.\n")
	b.WriteString("- The expansions of includes and uses share a budget: more than 100000 elements, 16 MiB of placed source, or 256 levels of nesting is `V021` at the include or use that went over, which inserts nothing and stops every later one; a fragment an `<include>` places inside a `<template>` has a budget of its own (\"exceeds the expansion limit for template definitions\"). `V019` names a simple cycle through the use, starting at its own template: up to 8 templates whole, else the first 8, `… (N more)`, and the template it returns to. A `with` path that is missing is one `B003` at the use (`with path \"form.phone\" (alias f) is missing`) and nothing more from the copy; `if`, `hidden`, `disabled`, `open`, and `class:NAME` read through an alias that stands for an object are null when the member is missing, without `B002`, while a `{path}` or a `bind` is `B003`.\n")
	b.WriteString("- A diagnostic about a path that went through an alias ends with `(P via <use id=\"U\">)`, where P is the path the alias stands for; a use without an `id` is named `<use template=\"T\">`, and ` at FILE:LINE:COL` follows when P starts with an `each` alias. Any other diagnostic about an element of a copy ends with `, placed by <use …> at FILE:LINE:COL`, and the location is the template's own line. An id, a path, or a template name a message quotes is cut at 64 bytes (at a character boundary) and followed by `…`.\n")
	b.WriteString("- The tools show the expansion. `tuimark inspect` ends with `source FILE:LINE:COL`, the element the node was built from, then one `via` line for each use or include that placed it, innermost first (`--json`: a `source` member `{file, line, col, via}` whose entries are `{use, template, file, line, col}` or `{include, file, line, col}`; a node the document wrote itself has `\"via\": []`, and a document that writes `version` has no `source`). `tuimark ir` keeps the composition as written: an `include` or `use` node holds the nodes it placed, in the template's own words (`f.value`, `{f.label}`) with scoped ids, each with a `from` member, `FILE:LINE`. `tuimark validate` of a fragment checks only its own elements, reads no file its includes name, and prints `ok (fragment checked on its own)` (JSON: `\"ok\": true`) with or without `--data`; `fmt` formats a fragment as a document with `<fragment>` as the root; `run` and `preview --watch` watch every fragment the last load read, at any depth, including one that does not exist yet; `tuimark_inspect` of a fragment returns the `V005` text as its result, not as an error. `tuimark lsp` gives a fragment the diagnostics the documents that include it give its file (found among the open documents and the `.tui` files of its directory and its parent), checks one no document reads on its own, follows `<include src>`, `template=`, and scoped ids across files for definition, and completes template ids and scoped ids.\n")
	b.WriteString("- Conventions for a reusable piece (a template and its uses):\n")
	b.WriteString("  - Name an id of a copy by its scoped id, `#U__x`, in selectors, `focus=`, `to=`, and `when`, and never `#U`: the use is not a node (`B005`, with the scoped id in the message).\n")
	b.WriteString("  - Pass data as a path: `with=\"form.email as f\"` makes `f` the path, not a value, so the template reads and writes `f.value` in place and a diagnostic names the real path. What a copy needs to vary is a member of that object.\n")
	b.WriteString("  - Vary one copy with a static `class` on its `<use>` (`class=\"wide\"`): every top-level element of the copy gets it, and the stylesheet styles `.wide`. A use takes no `class:NAME` guard.\n")
	b.WriteString("  - Pass a flag as an optional member of the `with` object (`f.required`, `f.error`): when the member is missing, `if`, `hidden`, `disabled`, `open`, and `class:NAME` read it as null with no diagnostic, so a copy whose object omits it has the flag off. A `{path}` or a `bind` on a missing member is `B003`.\n")
	b.WriteString("  - Write the size of every template root (`<row style=\"height: 1\">`): a `col` or `row` root is `1fr` only directly under a `screen`, a `modal`, or a `tab`, and content-sized anywhere else, so the same template takes different sizes in different places (see the defaults of the current language).\n")
	b.WriteString("  - Read a diagnostic in a copy by its end: `, placed by <use …> at FILE:LINE:COL` names the use, and the location before it is the template's own line.\n")
	b.WriteString("- The rest of the current language: its layout and key defaults are in the next section; the form controls and `{path}` in a `<button>` are in Notes; the spinner and `play`'s `tick:DUR` step, which advances it, are in the v0.2a `play` bullet.\n\n")
}

// writeNotes04b appends the 0.4b clarification to the Notes: a short word on
// composition (the current language's defaults are a section of their own).
func writeNotes04b(b *strings.Builder) {
	b.WriteString("- **Composition, briefly.** In a `<tui>` without `version`, `<include src>` places the elements of a `<fragment>` file where it stands, and `<template id>` with `<use template with>` places a copy of a piece of markup with its ids scoped by the use (`U__x`) and its data behind an alias (`with=\"path as alias\"`). The copy is part of the document the dump, the keymap, focus, and events see, so a reusable form field is a template and a long document is split into fragments. Read the v0.4b section above for the rules, limits, and messages, and `tuimark inspect` (`source`/`via`) or `tuimark ir` (`from`) for where a node came from.\n")
}
